  "comments": [
    {
      "path": "app/src/full/java/com/nuvio/tv/updater/model/AppUpdate.kt",
      "content": "`serverTimeMs` is the server's time at the moment the response arrived, and it only means something for that response. But `AppUpdate` gets persisted: `UpdateCheckWorker` saves the whole object with `prefs.setPredownload(..., encodeToString(update))`. So the cached pre-download JSON now also stores a server time that stops moving at fetch time. Nothing reads it from the cache today, because every `SilentClock.nowFor` call site uses the live result. Still, if any code later passes a cached `AppUpdate` to `nowFor`, \"now\" would be stuck at the fetch time and the 24 h wait and 72 h net would never pass. Marking the field `@Transient` (it already has a default) keeps it out of the cache and blocks this mistake.",
      "suggestion_code": "    @kotlinx.serialization.Transient\n    val serverTimeMs: Long? = null",
      "existing_code": "    val serverTimeMs: Long? = null",
      "start_line": 87,
      "end_line": 87,
      "category": "maintainability",
      "severity": "low"
    },
    {
      "path": "app/src/full/java/com/nuvio/tv/updater/AppVisibilityTracker.kt",
      "content": "Only `dispatchKeyEvent` counts as activity. Air-mouse remotes are common on Android TV boxes, and their pointer movement and clicks come through `dispatchGenericMotionEvent` and `dispatchTouchEvent`, not as key events. Touch-capable boxes work the same way. A member who browses with a pointer and has no audio playing (menus, settings, the search screen) still looks idle after 3 hours. The idle-on-screen path would then install and kill the app while they are using it. The new test pins this behaviour (\"Only key events count as a press\"). I suggest recording these input paths too, since the cost is the same: one volatile write.",
      "suggestion_code": "    override fun dispatchKeyEvent(event: KeyEvent): Boolean {\n        keys.pressed(clock())\n        return original.dispatchKeyEvent(event)\n    }\n\n    override fun dispatchTouchEvent(event: MotionEvent): Boolean {\n        keys.pressed(clock())\n        return original.dispatchTouchEvent(event)\n    }\n\n    override fun dispatchGenericMotionEvent(event: MotionEvent): Boolean {\n        keys.pressed(clock())\n        return original.dispatchGenericMotionEvent(event)\n    }",
      "existing_code": "    override fun dispatchKeyEvent(event: KeyEvent): Boolean {\n        keys.pressed(clock())\n        return original.dispatchKeyEvent(event)\n    }",
      "start_line": 83,
      "end_line": 86,
      "category": "bug",
      "severity": "medium"
    },
    {
      "path": "app/src/full/java/com/nuvio/tv/updater/SilentInstallWorker.kt",
      "content": "`DELAY_MS` and `SilentInstallDecision.OUT_OF_SIGHT_MS` are two separate literals that must stay equal. This PR had to change both, plus a separate test for each. WorkManager also computes the delay from `System.currentTimeMillis()` at enqueue time, while `quiet()` measures `elapsedRealtime` from the stored stop time. With zero margin, a small clock adjustment or a scheduling skew can run the job a few ms early. The job then logs APP_RECENTLY_ON_SCREEN and nothing retries until the next 6 h check. Derive the delay from the constant and add a small margin.",
      "suggestion_code": "        const val DELAY_MS = SilentInstallDecision.OUT_OF_SIGHT_MS + 5_000L",
      "existing_code": "        const val DELAY_MS = 900_000L",
      "start_line": 35,
      "end_line": 35,
      "category": "maintainability",
      "severity": "low"
    },
    {
      "path": "app/src/testFull/java/com/nuvio/tv/updater/SilentInstallDecisionTest.kt",
      "content": "`now` is `10_000_000L`, which is less than `IDLE_ON_SCREEN_MS` (10_800_000). So `now - idleMs` is -800_000, `now - 4 * 3_600_000L` is -4_400_000, and the key press is set to -805_000. `elapsedRealtime()` never returns a negative value, so none of these inputs can happen on a box: it has only been up for about 2.8 h, yet the tests call it idle for 3 h. The tests pass only because `latestUpTo` keeps negative values (they are ≤ now). They don't cover the realistic case where `lastStart`/`lastKeyPress` are null or dropped, `lastActive` falls back to 0 (boot), and `now` \u003c 3 h, which should give APP_ON_SCREEN. Use a larger `now` for the idle-on-screen tests (e.g. `20_000_000L` or more), and add a case for the boot fallback with `now` just under and just over `IDLE_ON_SCREEN_MS`.",
      "existing_code": "    private fun idleOnScreen() = quietInput().copy(\n        startedActivities = 1,\n        lastStartElapsedMs = now - idleMs,\n        lastStopElapsedMs = null,\n        lastKeyPressElapsedMs = now - idleMs - 5_000,\n    )",
      "start_line": 223,
      "end_line": 228,
      "category": "test",
      "severity": "low"
    }
  ],
